# Code documentation for {{ .Name }}

Write all code, comments and documentation in English. Use English kebab-case
names for documentation files; keep the conventional `README.md` entry point.

Each module includes a README with questions to resolve while implementing its
domain. `TODO(doc)` markers identify pending contracts; they do not describe
validation or guarantees automatically implemented by the generator.

- Document entity purpose and invariants.
- For use cases, describe authorization, inputs/outputs, errors and external effects.
- For repositories, specify isolation, concurrency, transactions and auditing.
- For adapters, document timeouts, retries, idempotency and connection ownership.
- For HTTP, document example payloads, permissions, pagination and error responses.
- For tests, use scenario names and explain only non-obvious doubles or boundaries.
  Keep tests next to the code.

Place Go comments next to declarations, starting with the identifier for exported
symbols. Explain intent and contracts rather than restating the implementation.
Examples must not contain secrets or personal data.

Update comments and tests whenever behavior changes. Record cross-module decisions
in `docs/decisions/` when needed, including context, alternatives, the decision and
consequences. Replace each `TODO(doc)` with concrete documentation when resolved.
